  "description": "Re-pollard of two Horse Chestnut trees (Aesculus hippocastanum) back to the established historic pollard points in accordance with BS3998:2010 recommendations. No felling proposed.\n\n\nReason for works:\n- To maintain the established pollard cycle.\n-To reduce mechanical stress and mitigate the risk of limb failure.\n- To manage the trees in line with their historic and ongoing management regime.\n-Works will return the trees to their previous pollard heads only, with no additional crown reduction beyond the existing framework.",
